<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  OBD Platform - Phase C: ESL configuration for a local SIP test endpoint.

  TEMPLATE - rendered at container start by infra/freeswitch-endpoint/scripts/entrypoint.sh.

  This exists only so the endpoint's OWN media statistics can be read during a
  test. A media claim is only two-way if the far end confirms it received
  audio, and the far end here is a container, so its counters have to be
  readable. See the comment on the published port in
  infra/docker-compose.freeswitch-endpoints.yml.

  THREE THINGS HERE WERE WRONG FIRST AND ARE THE REASON FOR THE COMMENTS
  Every one of them failed SILENTLY: FreeSWITCH started, reported itself UP,
  and simply ignored this whole file, leaving mod_event_socket on its compiled
  in defaults - which include the image's stock default ESL credential.

    1. The root element must be <configuration>, not <config>. mod_event_socket
       looks for a child element named "configuration" with name=
       "event_socket.conf". With <config> it finds nothing and keeps its
       defaults.

    2. The port parameter is "listen-port", not "port". With "port" the
       listener silently used the default 8021 by coincidence, so this mistake
       is easy to miss.

    3. There is no "bind-host" parameter. Setting one, alongside a correct
       listen-ip, is at best ignored; relying on bind-host alone is what left
       this endpoint listening on 127.0.0.1 and made the published port
       unusable.

  listen-ip is 0.0.0.0 for the same reason as on the platform switch: a
  published port is delivered to the CONTAINER's network address, not to its
  loopback, so binding 127.0.0.1 makes the published port accept a connection
  and then close it with zero bytes. The host-side mapping stays on 127.0.0.1,
  so the port is reachable from this machine only.

  Because an ignored settings file means the stock credential is live, the
  entrypoint's own refusal checks are the safety net: it verifies the rendered
  file really was produced before exec'ing FreeSWITCH, and a published ESL
  port that answers with a stock password should be treated as a defect.
-->
<configuration name="event_socket.conf" description="OBD Phase C endpoint Event Socket">

  <settings>
    <param name="nat-map" value="false"/>

    <param name="listen-ip" value="0.0.0.0"/>
    <param name="listen-port" value="8021"/>

    <!-- Rendered from the environment at container start; never committed. -->
    <param name="password" value="@@FREESWITCH_PASSWORD@@"/>

    <!-- Defence in depth: even though the published port is loopback-only on
         the host, restrict inbound peers to the private/loopback ranges in
         acl.conf.xml, exactly as the platform switch does. -->
    <param name="apply-inbound-acl" value="obd-dev-acl"/>

    <!-- Refuse to start the listener rather than silently continuing with
         defaults, which is how a stock credential could become live. -->
    <param name="stop-on-bind-error" value="true"/>
  </settings>

</configuration>
